      "role": "predictor",
      "is_predictor": true,
      "is_interpretable_segmentation": true,
      "rationale": "Derived from the incident description, problem_scope captures the breadth/locus of the issue (single_device, server_infrastructure, network_wide, multi_device_location). These are external, well-separated, interpretable categories that a human can segment on and compare against whether the incident is hardware-related. A scope like 'single_device' or 'server_infrastructure' plausibly co-varies with hardware problems versus 'network_wide' which may lean toward network/config issues, so it opens an informative relationship rather than merely restating the focus. Distribution is reasonably spread across categories, enabling meaningful comparison."
    }
  ],
  "n_predictors": 1,
  "relationship_informativeness": 0.7,
  "rationale": "The single added column is an associational, interpretable categorical variable extracted from the description that can be grouped and compared against the hardware_incident focus, satisfying the EDA claim. It does not restate the focus and its categories are well-separated with a usable distribution. Informativeness is capped below 1.0 because only one dimension of the description is surfaced, limiting the breadth of relationships an explorer could discover."
}

